<article class="env-remark" id="0CR2">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0CR2">Remark <span data-tag="0CR2">36.21.3</span>.</a> Let $X$ be a quasi-compact and quasi-separated scheme. Let $X = U \cup V$ with $U$ and $V$ quasi-compact open. By Lemma <a href="/tag/0CR0" data-tag="0CR0">36.21.1</a> the functors $DQ_ X$, $DQ_ U$, $DQ_ V$, $DQ_{U \cap V}$ exist. Moreover, there is a canonical distinguished triangle </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  DQ_ X(K) \to Rj_{U, *}DQ_ U(K|_ U) \oplus Rj_{V, *}DQ_ V(K|_ V) \to Rj_{U \cap V, *}DQ_{U \cap V}(K|_{U \cap V}) \to  \]
</div>
  <p> for any $K \in D(\mathcal{O}_ X)$. This follows by applying the exact functor $DQ_ X$ to the distinguished triangle of Cohomology, Lemma <a href="/tag/08BV" data-tag="08BV">20.33.2</a> and using Lemma <a href="/tag/0CR1" data-tag="0CR1">36.21.2</a> three times. </p>
</article>